summary:
- topic: Superintendent Search Update
  text: The Board announced that a robust search process has narrowed candidates to
    two finalists, and the Board has identified its preferred candidate. The Chair
    was authorized to enter into negotiations, with further information to be shared
    with the community once the process is complete.
- topic: Student Representative Farewell
  text: The Board bid farewell to student representatives Alex Davison and Angela
    Kabisa, commending their maturity, insights, and dedication during their tenure.
    Board members expressed appreciation for their contributions and wished them well
    in their future endeavors.
- topic: South Portland High School Top Scholars 2026 Recognition
  text: The Board recognized the South Portland High School Top Scholars for 2026,
    celebrating their academic achievements and extracurricular involvement. Students
    introduced each other, highlighting their accomplishments, community contributions,
    and future plans.
- topic: FY26-27 Budget Development and Audit Update
  text: The Finance Director provided an update on the FY26-27 budget, noting improved
    deficit projections and ongoing efforts to implement new payroll encumbrance software
    for more accurate financial reporting. She also clarified the multi-year effort
    required to resolve audit findings and improve internal processes.
- topic: MaineCare Billing for School Services
  text: The Director of Instructional Support presented on MaineCare billing, explaining
    the current process for occupational, speech, and physical therapy, and the complexities
    of parental consent and HIPAA regulations. She also discussed potential areas
    for expansion, such as day treatment and psychological evaluations, while highlighting
    associated regulatory and staffing challenges.
- topic: Policy Committee Updates
  text: 'The Policy Committee presented two policies for a first read: Policy BEDB:
    Agenda and the Educational Equity Policy. The Board approved both for further
    review, with discussions around ensuring the district has the necessary data and
    systems to effectively implement the Educational Equity Policy.'
- topic: Student Transportation Safety Concerns
  text: Public commenters and a student representative raised serious safety concerns
    regarding overcrowded buses for high school athletic events and daily routes.
    Students were reportedly standing in aisles and sitting on laps, prompting the
    Superintendent to commit to investigating the issue and providing a resolution
    report at the next meeting.
- topic: Kaler Elementary School Student Placement
  text: An update was provided on the placement of Kaler Elementary School students
    following its closure. The process is proving difficult due to uncertainties surrounding
    the long-term reconfiguration plan, but a survey was distributed to Kaler parents
    to gather feedback on their preferences for student placement.
